---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import EngagementPlanner from "../components/EngagementPlanner.astro";
import InquiryForm from "../components/InquiryForm.astro";
---
<Base
  wide
  pageClass="practice-page"
  title="Work with me"
  description="Private quantitative instruction, research-methods mentorship, and institutional training with economist and educator Ian Helfrich, Ph.D., from high school through professional practice."
>
  <header class="wp-hero" aria-labelledby="wp-title">
    <div class="wp-hero-folio"><span>PRIVATE PRACTICE · ST. LOUIS / WORLDWIDE</span><span>NEW INDEPENDENT ENGAGEMENTS</span></div>
    <div class="wp-hero-grid">
      <span>START WITH THE LAST STEP YOU TRUST</span>
      <h1 id="wp-title">Show me<br />where it <em>moves.</em></h1>
      <div>
        <p>The answer changes when you add a control. The code runs and the units are wrong. The exam is close and practice has stopped helping. Send me that point. We trace the reasoning backward until it holds.</p>
        <div><a class="ih-action" href="#planner">Find a starting point</a><a href="#inquiry">Go directly to inquiry →</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="wp-audience-rail" aria-label="Learners and clients served">
    <span>High school</span><span>Undergraduate</span><span>MBA</span><span>Graduate</span><span>Researcher</span><span>Professional</span><span>Team</span>
  </section>

  <div id="planner"><EngagementPlanner /></div>

  <section id="formats" class="wp-formats" aria-labelledby="formats-title">
    <header class="wp-section-head">
      <span>THE ENGAGEMENT LEDGER</span>
      <h2 id="formats-title">The price belongs<br />beside the work.</h2>
      <p>These are public starting points. Preparation, urgency, and organizational requirements can change a quote. You receive the scope, price, boundaries, and schedule in writing before paid work begins.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="wp-format-ledger">
      <article id="private">
        <span>01</span>
        <div><small>FOCUSED</small><h3>Private session</h3></div>
        <strong>$225 <small>/ 60 min</small></strong>
        <p>A defined concept, exam strategy, problem, code issue, model, or decision.</p>
        <ul><li>Brief intake</li><li>Prepared live instruction</li><li>Notes when useful</li></ul>
      </article>
      <article id="research">
        <span>02</span>
        <div><small>DIAGNOSE</small><h3>Methods diagnostic</h3></div>
        <strong>$325 <small>/ 75 min</small></strong>
        <p>A paper, thesis, dissertation, or applied project that needs a defensible route.</p>
        <ul><li>Advance review</li><li>Design session</li><li>Written roadmap</li></ul>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <div><small>ACCELERATE</small><h3>Four-week intensive</h3></div>
        <strong>From $1,800</strong>
        <p>A compressed runway for a course unit, qualifying exam, replication, or milestone.</p>
        <ul><li>Six sessions</li><li>Custom practice</li><li>Continuity between meetings</li></ul>
      </article>
      <article id="institutions">
        <span>04</span>
        <div><small>INSTITUTIONAL</small><h3>Team learning system</h3></div>
        <strong>From $5,000 <small>/ half day</small></strong>
        <p>Methods training paired with durable materials and the team’s real analytical context.</p>
        <ul><li>Needs analysis</li><li>Live workshop</li><li>Reusable infrastructure</li></ul>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="wp-rate-note">Existing arrangements remain under their current agreements. Work originating through Wyzant remains scheduled and paid there under platform rules.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wp-range" aria-labelledby="range-title">
    <header class="wp-section-head wp-section-head--inverse">
      <span>THE RANGE</span>
      <h2 id="range-title">SAT algebra to<br />CDE fixed effects.</h2>
      <p>I work across levels because the underlying task repeats: connect the intuition, formal object, implementation, output, and sentence someone has to defend.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="wp-range-matrix">
      <article><span>FOUNDATION</span><h3>SAT / ACT · AP · early research</h3><p>Error logs that record reasons, quantitative fluency that survives the test, sources with visible provenance, and an early path into data.</p></article>
      <article><span>COURSEWORK</span><h3>Economics · statistics · finance</h3><p>Micro, macro, econometrics, probability, corporate finance, capital markets, and MBA analysis taught as connected objects.</p></article>
      <article><span>INFERENCE</span><h3>Research design · causal methods</h3><p>Panel data, DiD, RDD, IV, event studies, synthetic control, experiments, diagnostics, and the limits on the claim.</p></article>
      <article><span>IMPLEMENTATION</span><h3>R · Stata · Python · Excel · Julia</h3><p>Data cleaning, reproducible workflows, visualization, geospatial analysis, replication, code review, and the bug nobody can find.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wp-boundaries" aria-labelledby="boundaries-title">
    <header>
      <span>FIT COMES FIRST</span>
      <h2 id="boundaries-title">You have to defend every line.</h2>
      <p>I will refer you elsewhere when the problem requires a different specialist, licensed advice, full-service execution, or time I cannot responsibly give it.</p>
    </header>
    <div>
      <article><span>STRONG FIT</span><ul><li>You want to understand how the answer is made.</li><li>The work involves quantitative reasoning, research, or implementation.</li><li>You are willing to show your process and revise it.</li><li>You value candor, preparation, and methodological care.</li></ul></article>
      <article><span>NOT A FIT</span><ul><li>You want graded work or an assessment completed for you.</li><li>You require a guaranteed grade, result, or publication.</li><li>You seek uncredited authorship or undisclosed analysis.</li><li>The engagement would violate an institution’s rules.</li></ul></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wp-process" aria-labelledby="process-title">
    <header class="wp-section-head">
      <span>THE PROCESS</span>
      <h2 id="process-title">Four steps.<br />Everything in writing.</h2>
      <p>You send the problem. I assess fit. We confirm the terms. Then the work begins with a shared definition of done.</p>
    </header>
    <ol>
      <li><span>01</span><h3>Send the real problem.</h3><p>Describe the work, what you have tried, the blockage, and the actual timeline.</p></li>
      <li><span>02</span><h3>Get a candid fit assessment.</h3><p>I reply with a format, a clarifying question, a referral, or an honest no.</p></li>
      <li><span>03</span><h3>Confirm the terms.</h3><p>Scope, rate, preparation, scheduling, cancellation terms, and integrity boundaries go in writing.</p></li>
      <li><span>04</span><h3>Hand the decision back.</h3><p>Every meeting ends with you making more of the next decision yourself.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="wp-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <header><span>BEFORE YOU ASK</span><h2 id="faq-title">Practical questions.</h2></header>
    <div>
      <details><summary>Do you offer reduced student rates?</summary><p>A small number of reduced-rate places may be available when capacity allows. Tell me honestly in the inquiry. Availability is not guaranteed, and urgent work is not discounted.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will you work directly in my code or data?</summary><p>Often, yes, alongside you and within an instructional or advisory scope. I demonstrate, review, debug, and explain. I do not quietly become the undisclosed analyst or author.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can you guarantee a grade, result, or publication?</summary><p>No. I can improve the quality of your reasoning, preparation, and execution. Outcomes still depend on your work, institution, data, and other factors neither of us controls.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do you meet remotely?</summary><p>Yes. Most work is remote and timezone-aware. In-person St. Louis engagements can be discussed when the format warrants it.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="inquiry" class="wp-inquiry" aria-labelledby="inquiry-title">
    <aside>
      <span>START HERE</span>
      <h2 id="inquiry-title">Tell me what<br />is at stake.</h2>
      <p>The useful details are the work, what you tried, where the reasoning breaks, and the real timeline.</p>
      <strong>I typically answer detailed inquiries within two business days.</strong>
    </aside>
    <InquiryForm />
  </section>
</Base>
